  "prompt": "Cosmic justice composition in the style of epic historical painting meets philosophical visualization: the ancient Shaolin Temple dissolves into fragments that reorganize into a massive cosmic wheel of karma, with each piece of fallen architecture becoming part of an enormous mechanism of universal justice. The composition shows the temple's destruction not as ending but as transformation into a greater pattern of moral law. Ultra-high-definition detail captures both the weathered stone of millennium-old architecture and the abstract geometric patterns of karmic cycles, rendered with equal precision and respect. Traditional Buddhist symbols--dharma wheels, lotus flowers, infinity knots--integrate naturally into the cosmic mechanism, while streams of cause and effect manifest as flowing golden threads connecting every element. The lighting design suggests both destruction and revelation--harsh light exposing hidden corruption contrasted with the gentle illumination of eternal justice. Color palette dominated by ancient stone grays and traditional Buddhist golds, with pure white light representing ultimate truth and justice. Particle effects show the temple's physical form dissolving but its essential elements reconstituting into eternal patterns of moral consequence. The background features both earthly temple settings and cosmic space, suggesting that individual actions participate in universal moral order that transcends any single institution or time period --ar 9:16 --raw",
